        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "deafc2dc-d56a-5f14-bd04-22a166f52c56",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Byrne, Shane Shu, Stephen Thomas Erlewine, Tom Petty, Van Morrison, Ben Harper, Robert Plant, Prince\n- Bands: Talking Heads, Blues Traveler, Sonia Dada, Widespread Panic\n- Radio Stations: KSPN-FM\n- Music Formats and Genres: AAA format, classic rock, new wave, punk, art rock, funk, world music\n- Places: New York City\n\nFacts:\n- Talking Heads were an American rock band formed in 1975 in New York City and active until 1991.\n- David Byrne, born on 14 May 1952, is a Scottish-born American musician who was the founding member, principal songwriter, lead singer, and guitarist of Talking Heads.\n- Talking Heads helped pioneer new wave music by integrating punk, art rock, funk, and world music with avant-garde sensibilities and an anxious, clean-cut image.\n- Critic Stephen Thomas Erlewine described Talking Heads as one of the most critically acclaimed bands of the 1980s.\n- KSPN-FM features the AAA format, combining classic rock artists such as Tom Petty, Van Morrison, and Talking Heads with newer musicians such as Ben Harper, Blues Traveler, Sonia Dada, and Widespread Panic.\n- Shane Shu's mezzo-soprano voice has been compared to David Bowie, David Byrne, and Robert Plant, and his dress sense has been compared to Prince.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
